  "question": {
    "text": "If the ratio of the roots of the equation \\(\\mathrm{px}^2+\\mathrm{qx}+\\mathrm{r}=0\\) is \\(a: b\\), then \\(\\frac{\\mathrm{ab}}{(\\mathrm{a}+\\mathrm{b})^2}=\\)",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "hH8GT",
      "text": "\\(\\frac{\\mathrm{p}^2}{\\mathrm{qr}}\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "dM632",
      "text": "\\(\\frac{\\mathrm{pr}}{\\mathrm{q}^2}\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "bf8D0",
      "text": "\\(\\frac{q^2}{\\mathrm{pr}}\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "dnfMe",
      "text": "\\(\\frac{\\mathrm{pq}}{\\mathrm{r}^2}\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hints: Let roots are \\(a \\alpha\\) and \\(b \\alpha\\)\n\\(\\Rightarrow(\\mathrm{a}+\\mathrm{b}) \\alpha=\\frac{-\\mathrm{q}}{\\mathrm{p}}\\)\n\\(\\begin{aligned} & a b \\alpha^2=\\frac{r}{p} \\\\ & \\frac{a b \\alpha^2}{(a+b)^2 \\alpha^2}=\\frac{r}{p} \\cdot \\frac{p^2}{q^2} \\\\ & \\frac{a b}{(a+b)^2}=\\frac{1 p}{q^2}\\end{aligned}\\)",
    "image": null
  },
